      "extracted_at": "2026-08-10T13:25:13Z",
      "payload": {
        "chunks": [
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Worldwide oil-equivalent production of 3.7 million barrels per day in 2025 was up approximately 12 percent from 2024, mainly due to the acquisition of Hess, completion of the Future Growth Project at Tengizchevroil (TCO), record production in the Permian Basin, and ramp-up of production in the Gulf of America, partially offset by asset sales in Canada and the Republic of Congo.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Acquisition of Hess Corporation",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "context": "proved reserves impact of Hess acquisition",
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "The largest additions were from the acquisition of Hess Corporation (Hess) and extensions and discoveries in shale and tight assets in the Permian Basin, and project approvals in Australia and Guyana. At December 31, 2025, 43 percent of the company's net proved oil-equivalent reserves were located in the United States, 15 percent were located in Australia and 11 percent were located in Kazakhstan.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Acquisition of Hess Corporation",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Chevron sold 70 percent of its working interest in Haynesville shale in East Texas in 2025 while retaining a 30 percent non-operated working interest and an approximately 12.5 percent overriding royalty interest in the newly formed joint venture. Chevron holds approximately 70,000 net acres and obtained a capital carry of $450 million for the development of this area through the sale transaction.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Haynesville Shale 70% Working Interest Sale",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In January 2025, the company sold its 31.5 percent nonoperated interest in the offshore Haute Mer permit area.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Republic of Congo Haute Mer Divestiture",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In January 2025, Chevron sold its interest in the ROC portion of Lianzi, while retaining the Angolan portion.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Angola-ROC Lianzi Partial Divestiture",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "geography": "Kurdistan Region of Iraq",
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2025, Chevron completed exit agreements and withdrew from the country.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Kurdistan Region of Iraq Exit",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "During 2025, the JDA Block A-18, acquired through the acquisition of Hess, was sold.",
            "entity_name": "CVX Malaysia JDA Block A-18 Sale",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "section_type": "Item_1",
              "update_type": "initiation"
            },
            "chunk_type": "guidance",
            "content": "The company estimates its average worldwide oil-equivalent production in 2026 to increase 7 to 10 percent over 2025, assuming a Brent crude oil price of $60 per barrel and excluding the impact of asset sales. This includes a full-year contribution from Hess assets. This estimate is subject to many factors and uncertainties, as described beginning on page 39.",
            "entity_name": "CVX FY2026 Worldwide Oil-Equivalent Production Guidance",
            "entity_type_entity": "GuidanceUpdate",
            "valid_from": null,
            "valid_until": null
          }
        ],
